          "text": "The Global Positioning System (GPS) is a constellation of orbiting satellites that provides position, navigation, and timing data to military and civilian users globally. ",
          "start": 74,
          "end": 245,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "The Global Positioning System (GPS) is a constellation of orbiting satellites that provides position, navigation, and timing data to military and civilian users globally."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-063728f3d9ea::sentence-8",
          "documentId": "doc-063728f3d9ea",
          "text": "The U.S. government provides civilian access to GPS on a continuous, worldwide basis, free of direct user fees. ",
          "start": 550,
          "end": 662,
          "contextSpans": [
            {
              "id": "doc-063728f3d9ea::sentence-9",
              "documentId": "doc-063728f3d9ea",
              "text": "It also provides open, free access to the information needed to develop GPS user equipment.\n",
              "start": 662,
              "end": 754,
              "direction": "NEXT"
            }
          ],
          "context": "The U.S. government provides civilian access to GPS on a continuous, worldwide basis, free of direct user fees. It also provides open, free access to the information needed to develop GPS user equipment."
